   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": "## References\n\n- Berger, M. (1987) *Geometry II*. Berlin: Springer. Chapters 14–15 classify conics and quadrics over $\\mathbb R$, including the projective refinement used in 2.04.\n- Coxeter, H.S.M. (1969) *Introduction to Geometry*. 2nd edn. New York: Wiley. Chapters 6 and 18.\n\nThe spectral theorem and Sylvester's law of inertia are assumed here; see [linalg-journey](https://github.com/cmsd2/linalg-journey) Stage 3, or:\n\n- ★ Olver, P.J. and Shakiban, C. (2018) *Applied Linear Algebra*. 2nd edn. Cham: Springer. Chapters 3–4 and 8.\n\nThe connection flagged to the shape operator of a surface is made precise in 3.04; see ★ Lee, J.M. (2018) *Introduction to Riemannian Manifolds*. Cham: Springer. doi:10.1007/978-3-319-91755-9.\n- Samuel, P. (1988) *Projective Geometry*. Undergraduate Texts in Mathematics. New York: Springer. ISBN 978-0-387-96752-3. Chapter 4 for the projective classification of conics.\n\n---\n*Marked ★ = in the local indexed library (`maths` collection); the rest are standard references given from knowledge, not consulted here. Every code cell in this notebook was executed and its output is the real result; the prose is written from knowledge and checked against these sources where they cover the material.*",
   "metadata": {}
